    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nwhen a line needs wrapping and you are have `set wrap` configured  ,  scrolling a file down with `j` sorts of stop scrolling for a while ,  issue is gone when mini.animate is not loaded\n\n### Reproduction\n\n- Scroll from top to bottom a file with lines that need wrapping using `g` ,  when `set nowrap` is set there's no issues.\nI'll attach a video to this tomorrow.",
