            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nYeah, I can reproduce this. I believe this is similar to #242 and the gist of the issue is [described here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/242#issuecomment-1446010930). As in:\n- First `j` initiates scroll. This puts cursor back on its starting position (at the time of pressing `j`).\n- Animation waits for some time before making scrolling a single step.\n- Second and other `j` is pressed and *again initiates scroll*. This stops the previous one and re-initiates the scroll: put cursor again on the previous position and wait.\n- And so on.\n\nFollowing [this advice](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/242#issuecomment-1446046151) fixes this particular issue as it makes the single animation step not be longer than key-repeat for `j` (which is OS specific). I'll take a look into maybe making this default and configurable.",
